### Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a “card” (a rectangular block with some content) that flips/rotates when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣  Container (perspective) ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  perspective: 1000px;          /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
  margin: 50px auto;            /* center horizontally */
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣  The card itself ---------- */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;  /* keep children in 3D space */
  transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* smooth animation */
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣  Front & Back faces ---------- */
.card .face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide backside when rotated */
  border-radius: 12px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

.card .front {
  background: #fff;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #333;
}

.card .back {
  background: #4a90e2;
  color: #fff;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);    /* start flipped */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣  Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* flip on hover */
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="face front">
      Front Side
    </div>
    <div class="face back">
      Back Side
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **1** | `perspective` on the wrapper creates a 3‑D context. |
| **2** | `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps child elements in 3‑D space. |
| **3** | Two faces (`front` and `back`) are positioned absolutely. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the face that is turned away from the viewer. |
| **4** | On hover, the whole card rotates 180° around the Y‑axis, revealing the back face. |

#### Customization tips

- Change `rotateY(180deg)` to `rotateX(180deg)` for a vertical flip.
- Adjust `perspective` value for more or less depth.
- Replace the text inside `.front` and `.back` with images, icons, or any HTML you like.
- Add `border`, `box-shadow`, or `background-image` to style the card further.

Enjoy your rotating card!
